  "id": "Compound::DB00589 - Gene::150",
  "verbalization": "Lisuride appears to interact with Adra2a through a shared pathway involving Adra2b, which participates in multiple receptor activities. The evidence suggests that Lisuride binds to Adra2b, which in turn is involved in Alpha2-adrenergic or Alpha-adrenergic receptor functions, both of which are participated by Adra2a. This implies a potential mechanism where Lisuride influences Adra2a through its interaction with Adra2b, possibly modulating receptor activity. The overlapping participation of Adra2b in different receptor activities highlights a possible functional link between Lisuride and Adra2a, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a role for Lisuride in modulating Adra2a through Adra2b, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct relationship.",
